{"name":"Coconut Ice","hex":"#ddd4c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coconut ice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chewy form of British confectionery prepared with grated (often desiccated) coconut, condensed milk, and sugar, and often coloured pink and white."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coconut_ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coconut ice","blocks":[{"text":"Coconut ice is a British solid soft confectionery prepared using grated desiccated coconut or just grated coconut, condensed milk and sugar. It typically has a chewy, soft and mildly grainy texture; some versions are semi-hard. Coconut ice is also available in South Africa, some areas of Australia, and New Zealand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Coconut_ice.jpg/330px-Coconut_ice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut_ice"},{"title":"Coconut","blocks":[{"text":"The coconut is a member of the palm family (Arecaceae) and the only living species of the genus Cocos. The term \"coconut\" can denote the whole coconut palm tree or the large hard fruit. Originally native to the Southeast Asia, New Guinea, and the Southwestern Pacific, they are ubiquitous in coastal tropical regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg/330px-Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Sundaes-Neopolitan-Coconut-Candies.jpg/500px-Sundaes-Neopolitan-Coconut-Candies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Sundaes-Neopolitan-Coconut-Candies.jpg/1280px-Sundaes-Neopolitan-Coconut-Candies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Sundaes-Neopolitan-Coconut-Candies.jpg/500px-Sundaes-Neopolitan-Coconut-Candies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American candy made by Brach's","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASundaes-Neopolitan-Coconut-Candies.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Coconut_4.jpg/500px-Coconut_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Coconut_4.jpg/1280px-Coconut_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Coconut_4.jpg/500px-Coconut_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoconut_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Sea_View_from_himsori_bangladesh_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Sea_View_from_himsori_banglades